X:1
T:Nocturne Op. 9 No. 2
C:Frédéric Chopin
O:Nocturne in E-flat major, Op. 9 No. 2
N:The theme and its first ornamented return (8 bars). Transposed down a minor seventh
N:from E-flat major to F major, so the lowest note is C4 and the highest E5.
N:Notes from three Humdrum first-edition encodings (ifdo.ca, kern2abc) that agree
N:bar for bar, and the flutetunes.com MIDI. The grace-note turn in bar 2, the mordent
N:signs in bars 5 and 6 and the grace notes in bars 7 and 8 are left out; the
N:trill in bar 7 is marked. In the
N:last bar the two lead-in eighths are replaced by a rest, so the tune comes round
N:evenly. Bar 6 has two D-flats, as in the MIDI and in the later reprise; the
N:first editions print D natural there. Chords from the left hand of the
N:flutetunes.com arrangement.
M:12/8
Q:3/8=44
L:1/8
K:F
